.TH "MEDIADEVICEINFO.TOJSON" "3JS" "October 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
MediaDeviceInfo.toJSON \- MediaDeviceInfo: toJSON() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]toJSON()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]MediaDeviceInfo\f[R] interface returns a JSON\-serializable plain
object representing the \f[CR]MediaDeviceInfo\f[R] object.
.PP
The method is automatically called by \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R] when a
\f[CR]MediaDeviceInfo\f[R] object is encountered during JSON
serialization.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toJSON()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A JSON\-serializable plain object containing the following properties:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]deviceId\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]kind\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]label\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]groupId\f[R]
.PP
Each property\(cqs value is copied as\-is.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Calling toJSON() directly
This example obtains a \f[CR]MediaDeviceInfo\f[R] object.
Calling \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] directly returns a plain object.
Its properties have the same values as the corresponding properties of
the original object.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]if\f[R] (!navigator.mediaDevices || !navigator.mediaDevices.enumerateDevices) {
  console.log(\(dqenumerateDevices() not supported.\(dq);
} \f[B]else\f[R] {
  \f[I]// List cameras and microphones.\f[R]
  navigator.mediaDevices
    .enumerateDevices()
    .then((devices) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
      devices.forEach((device) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
        \f[B]const\f[R] json = device.toJSON();
        console.log(json); \f[I]// A plain object\f[R]
        console.log(\f[B]typeof\f[R] json); \f[I]// \(dqobject\(dq\f[R]
        console.log(json.deviceId); \f[I]// Same value as device.deviceId\f[R]
      });
    })
    .catch((err) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
      console.log(\(ga${err.name}: ${err.message}\(ga);
    });
}
.EE
.SS Serializing to a JSON string
Within the \f[CR]forEach()\f[R] callback from the previous example, the
same object can be serialized using \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R], which
calls the \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] method automatically.
.IP
.EX
console.log(JSON.stringify(device));
.EE
.PP
This would log a JSON string like so (formatted for readability):
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqdeviceId\(dq: \(dqHJtTemQTM64Bivxv3ZEyKjCi1VR8042lPNpmXKObKJE=\(dq,
  \(dqkind\(dq: \(dqvideoinput\(dq,
  \(dqlabel\(dq: \(dq\(dq,
  \(dqgroupId\(dq: \(dqOkm2l1YZTrwy8awTxE8QSLNFoVMdIXx++wLh68tbmv0=\(dq
}
.EE
.PP
Each additional device is logged as a separate JSON string.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]JSON\f[R]
